# Frontend tests

- **Runner / DOM**: Vitest + jsdom; config under `test` in **`vite.config.ts`** (`include`: `src/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}`).
- **Setup**: **`src/test/setup.ts`** — `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` matchers.
- **Placement**: colocate `*.test.ts(x)` next to the module under test.
- **Coverage**: `npm run test:coverage` — thresholds in `vite.config.ts`; reports under `coverage/` (gitignored). CI runs the same command.
- **Workspace / sync**: prefer patterns in `context/WorkspaceContext.test.tsx` — mock `workspaceStorage` / `supabaseClient` with `vi.mock` + `vi.hoisted`; do not hit a real Supabase project in unit tests.
- **Editor / TipTap**: extend existing editor and `lib/pageDocument/*` tests when changing serialization or menus; see **`.cursor/skills/editor-tiptap/SKILL.md`**.
- **Router**: import `MemoryRouter` / route helpers from **`react-router`** (v8; not `react-router-dom`).
- **Generation**: follow **`.cursor/skills/musing-vitest-tests/SKILL.md`** when writing or updating suites.

## Anti-patterns

- Real network calls to Supabase or external APIs in unit tests.
- Asserting TipTap/ProseMirror internals instead of stored blocks, visible UI, or public helpers.
